{{!-- A dungeon exploration's rows, drawn inside the tracker's one `<ol>` (the part may produce a
      single top-level element, so everything here is an `<li>`).

      Three headed blocks, in the order of `procedures.md` → Dungeon Exploration Cycle: the party
      declaring and being resolved, the ongoing work, and the Dungeon Event. The cycle itself is
      the header's help mark. Nothing here rolls, gates or decides on anyone's behalf.

      Before Begin Exploring there is no turn, so nothing that belongs to one is drawn: no
      declaration, no narrated mark, no Dungeon Event. The cycle begins with the Warden's
      description, and a declaration made ahead of it would have no cycle to belong to. --}}
{{!-- A fight breaks out: a second combat with the party already in it. This exploration stays as
      it is and becomes the active one again when that fight is deleted. First in the panel, over
      the party, so it is never pushed down out of reach by a long list of work. --}}
{{#if dungeon.warden}}
    <li class="cairn-dungeon-fight-row">
        <button type="button" class="cairn-dungeon-fight" data-action="startFight">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-swords" inert></i>{{localize "CAIRN.Dungeon.Fight"}}
        </button>
    </li>
{{/if}}

<li class="cairn-combat-side cairn-dungeon-block">{{localize "CAIRN.Dungeon.Party"}}</li>

{{#each dungeon.rows}}
    <li class="combatant cairn-dungeon-row {{css}} {{#if resolved}}is-resolved{{/if}} {{#if panicked}}is-panicked{{/if}} {{#if deprived}}is-deprived{{/if}}"
        data-combatant-id="{{id}}" data-action="activateCombatant">

        <img class="token-image" src="{{img}}" alt="{{name}}" loading="lazy">

        {{!-- One grid: the edit glyph, the name with this turn's distance and the undo, then
              what the player declared — or, to the player who owes it, the button that asks —
              under the name, then the work they lend a hand to. The 20px slots are kept when
              empty, so every row's names, distance and glyphs sit in the same columns. --}}
        <div class="token-name cairn-dungeon-body">
            <strong class="name" data-tooltip-text="{{name}}">{{name}}</strong>

            {{!-- The pace is a hue — within torchlight, past it, past the three torchlights an
                  action covers — and past torchlight a glyph as well, so it never rests on colour
                  alone. --}}
            <span class="cairn-combat-moved {{#if pace}}is-{{pace}}{{/if}}" data-tooltip
                  aria-label="{{localize paceLabel}}">
                {{#if beyond}}<i class="fa-solid fa-person-running" inert></i>{{/if}}{{moved}}&nbsp;{{units}}
            </span>

            {{!-- Back to where the token stood when the turn began: core's recorded-movement undo,
                  for whoever owns the token — its player on their own row, the Warden on every row. --}}
            <span class="cairn-combat-slot is-undo">
                {{#if canRevert}}
                    <button type="button" class="inline-control combatant-control icon fa-solid fa-rotate-left"
                            data-action="revertMovement" data-tooltip
                            aria-label="{{localize "CAIRN.Dungeon.RevertMovement"}}"></button>
                {{/if}}
            </span>

            {{#if @root.dungeon.started}}
            {{#if prompt}}
                <button type="button" class="cairn-dungeon-declare" data-action="declareDungeon">{{localize "CAIRN.Dungeon.DeclarePrompt"}}</button>
            {{else if declared}}
                <p class="cairn-declared">{{declared}}</p>
            {{else}}
                <p class="cairn-declared is-waiting">{{localize "CAIRN.Dungeon.Waiting"}}</p>
            {{/if}}
            {{/if}}

            <span class="cairn-combat-slot is-edit">
                {{#if (and isOwner @root.dungeon.started)}}{{#unless prompt}}
                    <button type="button" class="inline-control combatant-control icon fa-solid fa-feather"
                            data-action="declareDungeon" data-tooltip
                            aria-label="{{localize "CAIRN.Dungeon.DeclareEdit"}}"></button>
                {{/unless}}{{/if}}
            </span>

            {{#if task}}
                <span class="cairn-dungeon-helping">{{localize "CAIRN.Dungeon.Helping" task=task}}</span>
            {{/if}}
        </div>

        {{!-- Narrated: the Warden's own mark of whose action has been resolved at the table —
              everyone acts at once in the fiction, and the Warden still talks to one player at a
              time. The system's toggle (Primitive 5) as a `<button role="switch">`, because core's
              `activateCombatant` selects and pans to the token on any click in the row that is
              not on an input or a button. Everyone sees the state; only the Warden sets it. --}}
        <div class="cairn-combat-acted">
            {{#if @root.dungeon.started}}
            <button type="button" class="cairn-switch cairn-acted-switch" role="switch"
                    aria-checked="{{#if resolved}}true{{else}}false{{/if}}"
                    data-action="toggleResolved" data-tooltip
                    aria-label="{{localize (ifThen resolved "CAIRN.Dungeon.NarratedUndo" "CAIRN.Dungeon.Narrated")}}"
                    {{#unless @root.dungeon.warden}}disabled{{/unless}}>
                <span class="cairn-switch-track"><span class="cairn-switch-knob"></span></span>
            </button>
            {{/if}}
        </div>
    </li>
{{/each}}

{{!-- Ongoing work: what takes several turns of effort, which several characters can share in one
      turn. The Warden names it and fills the turns in by hand; the players choose it in their
      declaration. Shown to the players only when there is some. --}}
{{#if (or dungeon.warden dungeon.tasks.length)}}
    <li class="cairn-combat-side cairn-dungeon-block cairn-dungeon-tasks-head">
        <span>{{localize "CAIRN.Dungeon.Tasks"}}</span>
        {{#if dungeon.warden}}
            <button type="button" class="inline-control icon fa-solid fa-plus" data-action="addTask"
                    data-tooltip aria-label="{{localize "CAIRN.Dungeon.AddTask"}}"></button>
        {{/if}}
    </li>
    <li class="cairn-dungeon-tasks">
        {{#each dungeon.tasks}}
            <div class="cairn-dungeon-task" data-task-id="{{id}}">
                <div class="cairn-dungeon-task-name">
                    <strong>{{name}}</strong>
                    {{#if @root.dungeon.warden}}
                        <button type="button" class="inline-control icon fa-solid fa-xmark" data-action="deleteTask"
                                data-tooltip aria-label="{{localize "CAIRN.Dungeon.DeleteTask"}}"></button>
                    {{/if}}
                </div>
                <div class="cairn-dungeon-marks" role="group" aria-label="{{progress}}">
                    {{#each marks}}
                        {{#if @root.dungeon.warden}}
                            <button type="button" class="cairn-dungeon-mark {{#if done}}is-done{{/if}}"
                                    data-action="markEffort" data-index="{{index}}" aria-pressed="{{done}}"
                                    aria-label="{{localize "CAIRN.Dungeon.TaskMark" n=n}}"></button>
                        {{else}}
                            <span class="cairn-dungeon-mark {{#if done}}is-done{{/if}}"></span>
                        {{/if}}
                    {{/each}}
                </div>
                {{#if helpers}}
                    <span class="cairn-dungeon-helpers">{{localize "CAIRN.Dungeon.TaskHelpers" names=helpers}}</span>
                {{/if}}
            </div>
        {{/each}}
    </li>
{{/if}}

{{!-- The Dungeon Event block is the Warden's alone (maintainer's call, 2026-10-16): the cost is
      said aloud at the table, and the panel is the Warden's reminder of it. The four triggers,
      one word each in a 2×2 grid, the full clause in the tooltip; a lit one is only a mark. Then
      the roll, and the costs the table charges. --}}
{{#if (and dungeon.warden dungeon.started)}}
<li class="cairn-combat-side cairn-dungeon-block">{{localize "CAIRN.Dungeon.Events"}}</li>

<li class="cairn-dungeon-close">
    <div class="cairn-dungeon-triggers">
        {{#each dungeon.triggers}}
            <button type="button" class="cairn-dungeon-trigger" data-action="toggleTrigger" data-key="{{key}}"
                    aria-pressed="{{#if lit}}true{{else}}false{{/if}}" data-tooltip-text="{{tip}}">{{word}}</button>
        {{/each}}
    </div>

        {{!-- Filled when something is lit, hollow when nothing is: the roll is always one click,
              and it is still there mid-turn — the Warden's Guide rolls in the middle of Freya's
              action, not at the end of the cycle. Beside it, the square picks the row instead. --}}
        <div class="cairn-dungeon-roll-row">
            <button type="button" class="cairn-dungeon-roll {{#unless dungeon.anyLit}}is-quiet{{/unless}}"
                    data-action="rollDungeonEvent">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-dice-d6" inert></i>{{localize "CAIRN.Dungeon.RollEvent"}}
            </button>
            <button type="button" class="cairn-dungeon-choose fa-solid fa-list-ul"
                    data-action="chooseDungeonEvent" data-tooltip
                    aria-label="{{localize "CAIRN.Dungeon.ChooseEvent"}}"></button>
        </div>

        {{!-- What the Dungeon Events table charges: Exhaustion's Fatigue and ration, Loss's
              light. Always there, because the fiction charges them on any turn; each asks who
              pays, so the Warden can let anyone off. Light reaches the lights the light-sources
              module keeps, which the system requires. The drawn event itself stays in the
              Warden's chat. --}}
        <div class="cairn-dungeon-costs">
            <button type="button" data-action="spendFatigue" data-tooltip-text="{{localize "CAIRN.Dungeon.FatigueTip"}}">{{localize "CAIRN.Dungeon.Fatigue"}}</button>
            <button type="button" data-action="spendRation" data-tooltip-text="{{localize "CAIRN.Dungeon.RationTip"}}">{{localize "CAIRN.Dungeon.Ration"}}</button>
            <button type="button" data-action="putOutLights" data-tooltip-text="{{localize "CAIRN.Dungeon.LightTip"}}">{{localize "CAIRN.Dungeon.Light"}}</button>
        </div>
</li>
{{/if}}
